WEBVTT

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.740
Hop, step, jump.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.640
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.450
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.900
Who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.150
They call me calm, strong, and cool. {cool de tsuyoku...}

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.500
Everyone says I'm popular.{iketeru to...}

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.910
But the truth is, I'm not like that at all. {honto wa...}

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.120
I'm just an ordinary girl! {futsuu ni...}

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.230
I wish I could just get rid {puressha nank...}

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.010
of all this pressure and be myself. {sunao ni naritai...}

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.850
But they'd all say it's out of character. {kyarajanai toka...}

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:03.260
Unlock my heart! {atashi no kokoro...}

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:08.610
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.460
Your Guardian Characters are with you. {shugo kyara ga...}

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.710
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.780
It'll be okay, really! {zenzen...}

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.690
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.460
Having only one style would be way too boring. {hitotsu...}

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.720
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.990
You can do anything! {nandatte...}

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.610
I know that...{kitto}

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.450
Hop, step, jump.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.340
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.210
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.520
...is who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:01:55.410 --> 00:02:00.780
They were both prodigies, and they both produced splendidly powerful X Eggs.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.900
I was able to gather some magnificent data thanks to them.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.160
Hello?

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.310
It's me. It would appear you have yet to find the Embryo.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.880
How long are you going to make me wait?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.320
Please don't be impatient. My current plan is progressing as we speak.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.900
The day when you'll be able to present the Embryo to the Boss is not far off.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.630
Your current plan?

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.130
It's something no one could even imagine.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.470
Let's just say a miracle is about to occur, and leave it at that.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.230
What kind of plan is it?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.040
I'll explain the details another time.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.670
Nikaidou, what are you thinking?

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.690
I wonder what his plan is.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.640
Nikaidou-san's?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.910
Does it matter?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.410
I'm not interested in anyone who puts on a fake smile.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.280
I'm not, and neither is Ikuto.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.400
I'll make an Embryo using the data I've collected.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.570
Yes, with my own hands.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.640
But before I do, I should get one more sample.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:27.350
I'll use the egg that is by far the most powerful as the test subject.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.250
My next target will be the Jack.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.580
Close Call at the Speech Contest!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.580
Episode 17

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.040
Tell me!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.940
Has all of this been your doing?

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:51.610
And if it has, what will you do?

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:57.830
Well, Himamori-san? {misspelling intentional}

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.890
What?

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.730
I'm pretty tough, you know.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.390
Amu-chan!

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.620
Wake up!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.420
This is the classroom!

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.900
Ouch!

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.650
So our representative will be...

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.360
Hinamori Amu-chan, of course!

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.500
Congratulations, Hinamori Amu!

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.630
What?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.270
Amu-chan, you were chosen to represent us at the speech contest!

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.040
Speech contest?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.010
We all voted on it.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.740
You got three more votes than Tadase-kun.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.300
You're really good, Hinamori Amu!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.880
Huh? Uh, thanks.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.030
How irritating! Why did I only get one vote?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.010
What? You're the representative?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.050
Congratulations, Hinamori-san.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.220
Good luck!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:05.410
It's just that Tadase's always been the representative, so we said they should pick someone less typical this year.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.370
Uh oh, the cat's out of the bag!

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.660
Who's "less typical?"

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.930
What's this speech contest, anyway?

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.740
Allow me to explain.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:22.240
The speech contest is a contest for speeches, held by Seiyo Academy Middle School.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.360
That doesn't really explain anything.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:29.140
Every year, the most outstanding honor students give speeches, then?!

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.760
Outstanding honor students?!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.640
Of course, only the best one wins.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.690
And one special representative from the elementary school participates.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:43.100
I-I'm not bragging, but I've never been chosen as an academic representative in my life!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.050
I can't give a speech! I can't even write one! No way!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.580
So why was I selected?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.850
Because you were napping.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.350
Napping?

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.490
Y-Yeah.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:59.530
I couldn't stop thinking about Nikaidou-sensei last night, so I didn't get any sleep.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.290
Then I just kind of...

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.190
This is the third day in a row that Nikaidou-sensei has been absent.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.290
Yeah.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:11.030
I was going to make him admit to being behind all the X Eggs.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.220
Yeah, yeah!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:17.170
He couldn't be planning on staying away to keep us from getting proof, could he?

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.580
No, as things are, I don't think he'd just go away.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.350
He'll probably come back with a new plan.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.250
We must be very cautious.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:33.310
Anyway, let's help Hinamori today!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.110
You have to draft your speech, right?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.310
Oh, yeah.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.920
The library should have records of all the previous speeches.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.270
All right! Let's go to the library!

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.510
Amu-chi! What's this year's theme?

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.050
"What you value most."

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:52.330
What you value most?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.250
What could that be?

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.180
It must be friends, don't you think?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.920
Friends! Yeah, I'll use that!

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.090
That settles it.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.050
What's wrong?

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.070
Nikaidou.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:06.510
Nikaidou?

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.810
I got the feeling he was here.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:17.070
What I value most right now...

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.510
Might possibly be...

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.990
Friends, maybe, but...

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.270
I also think that being stylish is important.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.680
But my allowance is really important, too.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:33.120
Ah! Something's just not right!

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:39.530
That's why I keep telling you that you should write about the importance of world domination.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.890
No, it's being the best in the world at soccer!

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:44.730
It's naps. Kids who take their naps grow up strong. {I know "stwong" isn't in there}

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.000
I want some paint.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.870
I would like a sewing set.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.550
I want, uh, um...

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.500
It's not about what you want, it's about what's important!

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.830
I would love to have a new kimono.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.860
I'm telling you...

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:59.940
Yes, the most important thing

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:03.640
must be the bonds of friendship, right?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.600
Jeez, you honor students...

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.030
What? I just think that no matter what kind of difficulties you face,

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.560
if you have friends, you can overcome them.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.080
Lame!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:15.690
What do you think it is, then, Soma-kun?

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:16.670
Me?

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.920
To give your all every day without regrets!

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.790
That's most important!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.090
You're too serious, Tadase.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.100
I am?

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.220
You two, listen to Amu-chan...

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.210
Oh, that's right.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.400
Ah, sorry.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.590
Hinamori Amu, once again you...

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.350
It's so frustrating!

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.680
My current favorite, Kukai-sama!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:43.200
And my previous favorite, Tadase-sama!

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.570
She's getting so close to them both!

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.680
Indeed.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.710
N-Nikaidou-sensei! Shouldn't you be on vacation?

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:55.020
Is something wrong, Yamabuki Saya-san?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.580
Nothing at all!

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.700
It certainly doesn't look that way.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:04.530
That Hinamori Amu really irritates me, too.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:09.350
Oh, why is that girl always around Kukai-sama and Tadase-sama?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.890
And I was the natural choice for the speech contest!

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.500
You're right, and it's important to honestly express your feelings.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:20.120
When you do, it makes your egg easier to manipulate. {Creepy!}

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.280
Now then...

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.460
See ya! Yeah. Wanna stop somewhere on the way home? {etc, in background}

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:37.730
The draft of the speech should be done. Nah, no way.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.560
Kukai-sama.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:43.340
Um, who are you again?

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:47.760
I am Yamabuki Saya, a close friend of Hinamori Amu-san's.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.090
We tell each other everything.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:51.240
Really?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.780
But I must admit, something has been bothering me.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.950
Hinamori-san has been saying some cruel things.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.010
Huh?

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:05.790
Like how you act so arrogant in front of Tadase-kun, even though you've never been chosen for the speech contest.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.550
Hinamori said that?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:08.980
No way.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:16.040
She says Tadase-kun is much better as a leader, so no matter how much you want the King's Chair, it's futile.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.480
I want the King's Chair?

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:22.590
Yes. She says it saddens her, as your friend.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.100
On top of that, even Tadase-sama...

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:29.100
Ah, you shouldn't read this letter!

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:42.720
"I put my experience to use to write Hinamori-san's draft,

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.710
but keep this a secret from Soma-kun.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.800
Soma-kun has never been chosen as our representative,

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:54.550
and I think he might have a complex because I'm the King's Chair, even though I'm younger than him."

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.010
Oh, there he is.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.630
Kukai!

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.800
Hey, the draft of my speech is finished. Take a look!

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:19.740
I've never wanted the King's Chair.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:20.600
Huh?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.310
And I don't have a complex about you either.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.060
What are you talking about?

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.520
Don't be so full of yourself.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:50.160
Man, I feel so betrayed. I can't believe he wrote that.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.820
Kukai.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.560
I trusted him!

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:57.350
Damn it. Who should I trust?

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.010
Daichi?

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.090
What's wrong, Daichi?

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.250
This can't be happening... My heart's egg...

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.350
Exactly what I was aiming for...

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:30.360
Soma Kukai, and the birth of the most powerful X Egg. {lit: highest energy}

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:44.370
{12:42, lines from right to left} 36th Seiyo Academy Middle School Speech Contest

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:49.020
The 36th Speech Contest will now begin.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.330
Six representatives have been selected!

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.710
In the end, who will claim the victory?

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.850
It'll be Hinamori-senpai, of course!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.710
I wonder what Hinamori-san's speech will be about.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.120
I can't wait!

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.750
Hinamori Amu will definitely win!

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:09.170
Ah, I can't take it, what should I do?! I can't do this!

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:10.440
Water!

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.510
I'm getting dizzy.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.540
Calm down, Amu-chan.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.740
Calm down.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.710
At times like this, you need the charm.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.580
That's right!

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.360
"No" character, "no" character... "Person," "person," "person!"

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:22.850
Fists!

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.330
Now you'll be okay.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:27.270
Yep. No, wait, I'm not!

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.980
You'll be fine. You can look at your script while you give your speech.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.260
Of course! Otherwise, I couldn't do it!

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.820
So you're really going through with it?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.850
You're going to read the speech that Tadase wrote?

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:45.480
Shouldn't a speech express your own feelings in your own words?

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:46.600
What?

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:53.380
Soma-kun, Hinamori-san wrote the speech herself. I only gave her a bit of advice.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.910
I know the truth, King's Chair. Who are you kidding?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.510
Kukai.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.820
Soma-kun, I think you're going too far.

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.350
How can you say that?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:10.100
Maybe you really do want the King's Chair.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.080
Well, maybe I'm a better choice for it than you.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.270
Hold on! Time out!

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:18.580
Calm down, Tadase-kun. And why are you mad, Kukai?

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.200
You keep quiet, Hinamori!

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.840
I won't! I can't!

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:26.850
Amu-chi...

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:30.370
They said your speech is the one after next.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.730
Okay.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.790
What I value most is working as hard as I can every day.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.950
The effort I expend to further my goals is more important than anything else!

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.420
Oh no, it's gone! Gone! Gone!

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:43.750
My speech is gone!

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:44.720
What?

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.500
I put it right in here!

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.000
Did you lose it?

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.420
Do you think...

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.720
Huh? He couldn't have...

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.580
Are you saying I hid it?

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:01.350
You were acting like you didn't want her to give her speech.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:04.230
I wouldn't do anything so mean!

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.610
Anyway, we have to hurry. It's almost your turn, Amu-chan.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:12.010
But I can't speak without the script.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.260
You must've dropped it!

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.830
What's going on, Tadase-kun, Kukai?

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.110
I can't stand to see you guys like that!

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:31.160
Damn, everyone thinks I did it.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:37.780
I can't believe I trusted them. What've I been doing all this time?

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:40.030
Guardians? Give me a break.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.420
Do you really hate your friends that much?

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:48.610
You really can't trust anything anymore.

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:49.940
Nikaidou!

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:55.080
It's natural for people to put themselves first.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.180
There's no such thing as friendship in this world.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.860
Isn't it refreshing to have it explained so clearly?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.120
Man, I don't understand anything anymore.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.450
I can't even believe in myself.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:21.670
That's fine. Your egg will make a wonderful X Egg.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.510
An X Egg?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.040
{Oof!} {What he says is the sound for expending a little energy. "Oof" is the best I could do in English, but I don't think it need to be subtitled.}

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:33.310
Caught you red-handed, Nikaidou!

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.730
W-What?!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.260
You're a pretty good actor, Soma-kun.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.450
Same to you, Tadase.

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:42.660
Huh? What?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:47.870
This is how he's been turning everyone's eggs into X Eggs.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.690
Now we've got proof! Everything that's been happening has been your fault!

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:57.870
Um, could someone please explain?

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.430
Tadase would never write a letter like this.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.670
If I couldn't figure that much out, I'm not fit to be a Guardian.

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:06.740
Soma-kun asked me about it immediately,

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:10.790
and that's when we concocted the plan to lure Nikaidou-sensei out.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:14.950
Did you know about this?

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.720
I didn't really know; it's more like I noticed.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.600
And after you left the room, she told me.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.270
What's up with that?!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.240
I'm sorry, but "to deceive your enemies, you must begin with your friends."

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.710
I won't forgive you this time!

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:32.250
So that's it, Nikaidou!

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:38.540
I'm me, and Tadase is Tadase. Being different is what makes things fun.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.010
And because we're opposites, we can help each other out.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:44.020
But fighting every now and then keeps things fresh.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.150
Maybe we should've made it a little flashier.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.300
You wanna go?

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:51.630
That's the Guardians for you.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.070
They complement each other perfectly.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.770
You can always count on them.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:55.670
Yeah.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:59.880
It looks like my time to leave this school has come.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.040
Ah well, I've no further use of this place,

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.140
and I did get this nice souvenir.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.330
What's that?

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:09.000
Data from the children at this academy.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:14.420
I believe it will prove useful to my research. Good-bye.

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:15.740
I won't let you go!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.130
Leave it to me!

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:20.750
You're pretty fired up.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:27.340
N-Not really. It's not like I'm mad that I'm the only one who didn't know about your plan!

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.090
That's bothering you, is it?

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.520
Um, sorry.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.270
Amu-chan, let's go!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:37.730
My heart: Unlock!

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:52.180
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.270
Heart Rod! {vroom!}

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:57.620
Heart Rod!

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:58.560
Amazing!

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.350
I wish I had a new item!

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:01.940
Finish this quickly!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:02.590
Right.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.480
But what's with this magical girl item suddenly showing up?

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.440
Nothing's coming out! The magic won't come out!

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.320
You're doing it wrong.

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:11.320
Oh, it was just a bluff.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:13.020
Oh, I see. I throw it.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.290
Correct!

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:18.360
Spiral Heart!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.420
Well, that was pointless.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:24.530
Just kidding!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.540
Just a little more!

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.310
I see. You're pretty good.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.910
I won't miss next time!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.560
Should you be doing this?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.990
Isn't it about time for your speech?

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:47.010
And now for our final entry: the elementary school's representative, Hinamori Amu-san.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.040
I forgot about the speech!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.090
I guess I'd better give this back, then...

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:55.490
Ah, the speech I worked so hard to write!

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:57.980
Character Change!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.010
Leave this to us!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.330
Hinamori-san, hurry back to the auditorium!

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.080
But I don't have my speech!

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:05.360
You'll think of something.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.480
Hurry!

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.180
Thanks, guys. Sorry for leaving you with this.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:11.630
Huh?

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:14.890
Shoot.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:16.190
Damn.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:21.220
Is Hinamori Amu-san absent?

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.500
What's she doing?

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.540
Hinamori-senpai?

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:31.100
Well then, everyone, I shall give a speech instead!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:40.100
So many eyes staring at me!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.720
M-My mind's going blank! What should I talk about?

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:54.220
A-A lot of things happened today.

00:20:55.220 --> 00:21:00.350
I even stupidly doubted my friends for a little while.

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:06.480
But now I know that you have to trust your friends.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.890
Trust your friends.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.230
Your friends...

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:10.380
Friends...

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:11.610
Friends...

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:14.270
T-That's all!

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.750
Wonderful! Cool & spicy!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.960
Exactly!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.030
Hinamori Amu!

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:23.750
You're the best!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:27.390
Huh? What am I doing here?

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:31.550
Oh my! Everyone's clapping for me!

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:42.350
The Embryo will soon be born. I will be the one laughing in the end.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:46.980
You did it, Amu-chan!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.450
{21:48} Judges' Special Award

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:48.830
You got the Judges' special award!

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.610
You were amazing!

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:52.580
Well done, Hinamori!

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:53.720
Congratulations.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.640
It was an excellent speech.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.910
I listened to every word! {lit: sat still and listened to the whole thing}

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:01.270
I-It's nothing worth making a fuss over.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:04.230
I'm going to engrave this feeling in my heart. {The verb is left out, so feel free to change it}

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:07.430
Someday, let's kick Nikaidou's butt together!

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:08.810
Yeah!

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:17.630
The hearts of the Seiyo Elementary Guardians are united!

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:41.890
Unless the world ends, I'll always {sekai ga...}

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:44.660
love you!  Yeah, you! {suki da yo...}

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:48.130
'Cause I just love, love, love you! {suki suki suki...}

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:52.860
Sure, I might struggle, but I'm still living. {jitabata...}

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:55.540
So figure it out already! Yeah, you! {kizukeyo...}

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:59.180
Even though I love, love, love you, {suki suki suki...}

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:05.370
I wanna say it but, shoot, I just can't! {iitaikuseni...}

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:09.490
I wanna show you what's in my heart! {tsutaetai...}

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:12.920
Oh yes! You're my one true hero. {oh yes!...}

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:18.080
Being in love's gonna be a bumpy ride.  {koishiterukagiri...}

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:24.010
But keep going! Okay, greenhorn rider? {hashitsuzukero...}

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:29.260
Straight down the path, into the sunset, stronger and stronger. {yuuyake...}

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:38.130
Ride through the wild land of youth. {seishun no...}

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:53.770
I'm so glad that Tadase-kun and Kukai weren't really fighting.

00:23:53.830 --> 00:23:56.130
It's best when everyone gets along!

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:59.330
Next time, the Guardians are going to the aquarium, right?

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:00.040
That's right.

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.730
I can't wait to see the dolphins!

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:07.490
I'm just going because everyone said they wanted to. I'm not particularly looking forward to it or anything.

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:09.830
There it is, Amu-chan's stubborn side...

00:24:09.910 --> 00:24:12.750
Next time on Shugo Chara: Happy and Embarrassing First Date!

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:15.590
Date? You mean it'll just be Tadase-kun and me?!

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:17.290
Oh man, what'll I do?!

00:24:17.340 --> 00:24:19.640
Amu-chan, calm down!
